Based on the empirical data from our closed-lost records, the primary driver for recent deal attrition is **Pricing**. 

While the volume of lost deals is currently low (1 deal), the "crm" opportunity was lost specifically because the cost did not align with the prospect's budget or perceived value. When deals are lost to pricing, it typically signals one of two commercial gaps:
